  "definition": {
    "id": "ACT-SPEAK",
    "instanceId": "EX-CORE-U5-42-required-speaking",
    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Speaking and interaction practice",
    "subtitle": "An interrupted cooking task",
    "context": "The reader identifies which action was interrupted and which observation prompted it. Express this outcome using the unit’s selected vocabulary and constructions.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U5-42-required-speaking-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Explain the situation",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U5-42-required-speaking-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "An interrupted cooking task: Present a supported viewpoint about the decision in this account. Refer to a concrete source detail, acknowledge a plausible alternative, and qualify what the evidence cannot establish.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "周末，我准备给朋友做饭，已经把蔬菜洗好，正要开始炒菜，却发现地面上有一小片水。我以为刚才洗菜时把水弄到了地上，没有马上注意。\n\n过了一会儿，水越来越多。我停下手里的事，先看看水从哪里来，发现放在旁边的锅还没有上火，里面的水却一直往外流。\n\n朋友建议把地面擦干就继续做饭。我摇摇头，说如果锅里的水还在往外流，只擦地面不能解决问题，地面有水，走路也不安全。\n\n我们先不用那个锅，把里面的东西移到另一个锅里，再把地面弄干净。因为还没有开始炒菜，换一个锅并没有让准备的食物浪费掉。\n\n饭做好以后，我把水会往外流的锅放在一边，写清楚不能继续使用，准备问专业人员是否还能修。朋友也帮忙看了其他东西，没有再催我快一点。\n\n吃饭时，大家只晚了一会儿。朋友笑着说，刚才确实应该停下来，不然我们可能一边做饭，一边不停地擦水，最后还是要重新处理这个问题。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Take your speaking turn",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed speaking practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "A concrete source detail supports my position."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I represented the alternative fairly and retained an important qualification."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
